<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Network_Test_Config.xml: optional latency measurements on the System information page.
  Off by default (Enabled="False"). Only administrators can change this file; users cannot add or change targets.

  The measurements run in the context of the user, only read, and send no data other than a name lookup,
  an ICMP echo request to the default gateway and the opening (and immediate closing) of a TCP connection.
  They run in the background together with the other system information.

  Settings
    Enabled    True switches the measurements on.
    Gateway    True (default) measures the round-trip time (ping) to the default gateway.
    Samples    Measurements per value, 1 to 5 (default 3).
    TimeoutMs  Wait time per measurement in milliseconds, 200 to 5000 (default 2000).

  Targets (up to 5)
    Label  Name shown in the list (letters, digits . _ - and space, up to 40 characters).
    Host   DNS name or IPv4 address. Choose the name according to what the measurement should show:
           - an internal name (reachable only in the company network or through VPN) shows the quality of the
             internal connection (office, VPN);
           - a name that is reachable from the internet shows the connection of a device that works remotely
             without VPN. Use an address that you operate or that is meant for such tests.
    Port   Optional (1 to 65535). With a port the time to open a TCP connection is measured too.
           Without a port only the name lookup is measured. For an IPv4 address no name lookup is measured.
  Entries that are not valid are skipped. Check the file with tools\Test-SelfXNetworkMeasure.ps1.

  Note on the DNS time: the name is resolved through the Windows resolver, so its cache applies. Repeated
  measurements can be faster than the first one.

  Example (remove the comment marks):
  <Targets>
    <Target Label="Intranet" Host="intranet.example.org" Port="443" />
    <Target Label="Internet" Host="www.example.org" Port="443" />
  </Targets>

  Citrix: add the address of the StoreFront server or the Gateway of the Citrix Workspace app as a target
  (for example Label="Citrix Gateway" Host="citrix.example.org" Port="443"). The row shows whether the name resolves
  and how fast the connection opens; users and the support team see it in the system information and in the ticket.
-->
<Network_Test_Config>
  <Settings Enabled="False" Gateway="True" Samples="3" TimeoutMs="2000" />
  <Targets>
  </Targets>
</Network_Test_Config>
